-- title:
--   Image of a special-fibre component is closed
-- statement:
--   Fix $N_0 \ge 1$ and a prime $q$ with $q \nmid N_0$, and let $\mathfrak X$ be a Deligne–Rapoport model package of level $(N_0,q)$, i.e. a term of `DRModelPackageLevel N₀ q hqN`. Let $O$ be a commutative local ring equipped with a ring homomorphism $\rho_O \colon$ `DRLevel.R q` $\to O$ whose maximal ideal is the principal ideal generated by the image of $q$, let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$, let `toκ` $\colon O \to \kappa$ be a ring homomorphism, and let $i \in \{0,1\}$. Write $\tau =$ `toκ`$\,\circ\,\rho_O$ for the induced map to $\kappa$; the scheme `DRLevel.fibre0 τ`, the fibre product of `toBase0 N₀ q` with $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\tau$, is integral by `𝔛.isIntegral_fibre0`, so it has a generic point. Consider the composite of the $i$-th component morphism `𝔛.comp κ τ i` with the base-change morphism `DRLevel.bcMap ρO toκ`, the map of fibre products given by the identity on $\mathfrak X$ and by $\operatorname{Spec}$ of `toκ` on the base, from the $\kappa$-fibre of $\mathfrak X$ to its base change `XO ρO` over $O$. The assertion is that the set-theoretic range of the underlying continuous map of this composite equals the closure of the singleton consisting of the image of the generic point of `DRLevel.fibre0 τ`, and that this range is a closed subset.
--
--   This identifies the image in $\mathfrak X \times_{\mathbb Z_{(q)}} \operatorname{Spec} O$ of each of the two components of the geometric special fibre of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_0(N_0 q)$ as the Zariski closure of the corresponding point $\xi_\infty$ or $\xi_0$, so in particular each component image is a closed irreducible subset. It is used in the analysis of the crossing of the two components, for instance in the descriptions of the maximal ideal at a crossing point and in the construction of oriented crossing charts.
